Longer messages for word wrap testing
producer:
  payload-template: |
    {
      "id": "{{i}}",
      "message": "This is a very long message for record {{i}} and it is intentionally large so that word wrapping, pagination, and fixed width generation can be stress tested properly in the batch flow."
    }
One important note

This uses:

kafkaTemplate.send(record);

which is fine for quick local load generation.

If later you want stricter testing, you can make it wait on each send result, but for now this is the simplest practical version.

Small improvement I’d suggest right away

If you want to avoid accidental huge sends during startup, set default as:

producer:
  enabled: false

and turn it on only when testing.
